                      <td>{s.traffic}</td>
                    </tr>
                  ))}
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </figure>

            <h2 id="pitch">The pitch that works for iGaming editors</h2>
            <ol>
              <li><strong>Lead with the data or the jurisdiction.</strong> "Our Q3 figures for the Ontario market" or "what the new Brazil rules mean for operators" earns the read on the trade sites.</li>
              <li><strong>Prove you are in the industry.</strong> A role at an operator, supplier, affiliate or law firm, or a track record of published analysis. Trade editors screen hard for insiders.</li>
              <li><strong>Pitch the section.</strong> "For your regulation coverage" or "for the affiliate desk" shows you read the publication.</li>
              <li><strong>Match the format.</strong> Trade sites want a tight, sourced analysis. Poker and betting sites want reported journalism or strategy. Review portals want a genuine guide.</li>
              <li><strong>Bring the assets.</strong> A data set, a chart, an executive quote, a jurisdiction-by-jurisdiction table.</li>
              <li><strong>Disclose the operator or affiliate tie</strong> up front. In a YMYL niche this is non-negotiable.</li>
            </ol>
            <div class="callout"><p><strong>The test:</strong> would a trade editor run this if you had no brand to promote? If yes, pitch it. If it is a list of your own bonuses, it goes in the bin.</p></div>

            <h2 id="mistakes">What not to do</h2>
            <ul class="check-list">
              <li>Buy links from casino blogs that quote a flat per-post price. That is the exact footprint Google penalises here.</li>
              <li>Pitch a regulator or responsible-gambling site anything with a commercial link.</li>
              <li>Send "top 10 online casinos" content to a trade publication. They cover the industry, not the promotions.</li>
              <li>Put exact-match anchors ("best online casino") on links back to your brand.</li>
              <li>Run AI-generated market analysis with no real figures and no named author. Trade editors spot it instantly.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="callout"><p><strong>Bottom line:</strong> in iGaming, a short list of placements on real trade and editorial sites beats a long list of affiliate links every time, and it is the only approach that does not put the domain at risk. Use this list to find the few that count.</p></div>
